Wait...you've...never heard of Pikmin? And yet you named...wow...  
You've just won Coincidence of the Year, my friend.

Pikmin was one of the Nintendo Gamecube's launch(or near launch)  
games, and it's one of the most fun games I've ever played. Think  
Harvest Moon(a farming/dating/cooking sim) crossed with SimAnt(and  
ant sim), and you might have an idea. It's about this guy named  
Captain Olimar that crash lands on a planet. He has to use these  
little plant/animal things called "pikmin" to help him find all of  
the parts to his ship and repair it. Fun game, and what with its age,  
it shouldn't be very expensive. Well worth any price, though.

A better review(with screenshots!) is at http://www.gamespot.com/ 
gamecube/strategy/pikmin/review.html

